# Per-machine configuration for the PULP/gvsoc target (RUNTIME=pmsis) on the
# lucap workstation. This is the machine with the GAP SDK + gvsoc simulator
# installed — the pmsis runtime only runs where those exist.
#
# Both run_correctness.sh and run_performance.sh read this file via common.sh.
# To use it, copy it to `config.env` (same directory):
#   cp config.env.pulp-workstation.example config.env
#
# `config.env` is git-ignored, so your local paths never get committed.
# Anything you export in your shell before running the script overrides these.
#
# The pmsis flow needs FIVE external pieces:
#   1. host LLVM/CIR tools (clang-cir, cir-opt, mlir-opt, mlir-translate)
#   2. the mlir-opt-omp build
#   3. a riscv32-capable LLVM opt/llc (xpulpv backend) for the kernel.o
#   4. the GAP SDK (sourced env) + the GAP RISC-V GCC toolchain on PATH
#   5. the PolyBench-PULP harness: a checkout whose PULP-SDK Makefile supports
#        make clean all run platform=gvsoc KERNEL_SRC=... [OMP_NATIVE=1|OMP_OPT=1]
#      and prints 'Cycles = N' after the run.

# --- Tool directories (prepended to PATH if set) ---------------------------
LLVM_BIN="/home/tagliavini/MLIR/INSTALL-LLVM/bin"    # clang-cir, cir-opt, mlir-*
OMP_TOOL_BIN="/home/tagliavini/MLIR/INSTALL-LLVM/bin"  # dir containing mlir-opt-omp
# GAP RISC-V GCC toolchain used by the PULP-SDK make (prepended to PATH):
PULP_TOOLCHAIN_BIN="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/gap_riscv_toolchain_ubuntu/INSTALL/bin"

# --- riscv32 backend (xpulpv) -----------------------------------------------
# The llc/opt that produce kernel.o. May be a different LLVM install than the
# host tools above (it needs the RISC-V + xpulpv backend). ADJUST:
PULP_OPT="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/llvm-project/builds/INSTALL-REBASE/bin/opt"
PULP_LLC="/home/tagliavini/toolchains/llvm-project/builds/INSTALL-REBASE/bin/llc"
# PULP_OPT_FLAGS=""    # host 'opt' pass on the .ll; none by default
# PULP_LLC_FLAGS="-O3 -mtriple=riscv32-unknown-elf -mattr=+m,+c,+xpulpv -relocation-model=pic"

# --- PULP harness ------------------------------------------------------------
# Directory with the PolyBench-PULP PULP-SDK Makefile. ADJUST:
PULP_APP_DIR="$HOME/PolyBenchC-PULP"
# The kernels live inside the same checkout, so point POLYBENCH at it too:
POLYBENCH="$PULP_APP_DIR"
# GAP SDK environment, sourced automatically by common.sh. Alternatively
# comment this out and source it yourself before running:
PULP_SDK_ENV="/home/tagliavini/gap8/gap_sdk/configs/gap8_v3.sh"
# PULP_PLATFORM="gvsoc"     # gvsoc | board
# Path (relative to PULP_APP_DIR) of the linked ELF, used for the size columns:
# PULP_BUILD_BIN="BUILD/GAP8_V3/GCC_RISCV_PULPOS/test"
# PolyBench defines baked into the opt kernel.o — MUST match what the harness
# Makefile defines for the native builds:
# PULP_POLYBENCH_DEFS="-DPOLYBENCH_DUMP_ARRAYS -DPOLYBENCH_TIME"
# PULP_VERBOSE=1            # stream the make/gvsoc output instead of logging only

# --- Paths -------------------------------------------------------------------
# RULES defaults to the repo's rules.dsl; override to pin another copy:
# RULES="$HOME/rules.dsl"
# OpenMP headers used by the clang->CIR front-end (workstation ships gcc-12):
INC_OMP="/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/12/include"
# OUTDIR="$PWD/results"

# --- Run parameters ----------------------------------------------------------
RUNTIME="pmsis"
# GAP8 memory is tiny: keep MINI, and it must match the dataset the harness
# Makefile compiles the native (ref) side with.
DATASET="MINI_DATASET"
SUITE="full"              # the harness checkout carries the full kernel set
# KERNELS="linear-algebra/blas/gemm/gemm-omp.c ..."  # explicit list overrides SUITE
# THREADS is ignored on pulp: the core count is fixed by the harness Makefile
# (NUM_CORES). REPS is ignored too: gvsoc is deterministic, 1 run per cell.
